## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of QUIC edge behavior, roaming networks, and realistic debugging plans.

## Key Concepts
- QUIC connection migration
- Edge CDN revalidation
- DNS path variation and ECMP

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-logic to correlate migration events from edge logs
function correlateMigration(logs) {
  const byCID = new Map();
  for (const e of logs) {
    if (e.type === 'migration') byCID.set(e.cid, e);
  }
  return byCID;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test QUIC migration behavior in a lab without affecting real traffic?
- What metrics would you alert on to detect roaming-related QUIC issues?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to diagnose production latency where security tooling (TLS inspection) interacts with edge caches and rate limits.

## Key Concepts

- TLS inspection overhead and queueing
- Firewall connection limits and burst behavior
- Edge CDN caching and TTLs
- Observability: edge logs, pcap, and curl timing data

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple latency probe using fetch
async function probe(url){
  const t0 = performance.now();
  await fetch(url);
  const t1 = performance.now();
  console.log('latency', t1 - t0);
}
probe('https://edge.example/login');
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify bypass granularity while maintaining security?
- What metrics would you monitor during a peak event to alert on this issue?
